== Re-bind, first attempt (tag 2026-11-06-b10; rebind-b10.stdout): STOPPED by its own check ==
rebind_evaluation.py asserts that only declared eligibility changes appear. It stopped at
"assert vs_hist == _counts(cumulative)": against the historical benchmark eligibility_reason differs in 416 rows,
where B5's inherited chain accounts for 208. Scored results had already been asserted unchanged. Measured with the
tool's own functions on the evaluation copy, against B9's package: vcf_sha256 1,456 rows and eligibility_reason 208
rows, all one change: CYP2D6, from "CYP2D6 copy-number and structural variation is not called from the uploaded VCF in
this application, so codeine guidance is not produced." to "... so codeine guidance is produced only from a CYP2D6
diplotype supplied by a dedicated caller (Cyrius, BCyrius, Aldy or StellarPGx)." The evaluation records the codeine
capability limitation as CYP2D6's eligibility reason; the plan declared that rewording for S1-S6 bodies but not here.
This fails the plan's zero-regression clause ("no eligibility or discrepancy change against B9's package") as
written. Stopped and asked, per the Part B rule. No package was written and no tracked file changed.

